        "section": "transkript"
      },
      {
        "id": 4,
        "title": "Refactor API Router Structure",
        "description": "Split the monolithic API into focused routers organized by domain, implement consistent endpoint patterns, and standardize error handling across all API endpoints.",
        "details": "This task involves restructuring the API router architecture to improve maintainability, readability, and consistency:\n\n1. Analyze the current API structure:\n   - Identify all existing endpoints and their functionality\n   - Group endpoints by domain/resource (users, products, authentication, etc.)\n   - Document current error handling approaches and inconsistencies\n\n2. Create domain-specific router modules:\n   - Implement a router factory pattern for consistent initialization\n   - Create separate router files for each domain area:\n     ```python\n     # /app/api/routers/user_router.py\n     from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException\n     from app.services.user_service import UserService\n     \n     router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/users\", tags=[\"users\"])\n     \n     @router.get(\"/\")\n     async def get_users(user_service: UserService = Depends()):\n         return await user_service.get_all_users()\n     \n     @router.get(\"/{user_id}\")\n     async def get_user(user_id: int, user_service: UserService = Depends()):\n         user = await user_service.get_user_by_id(user_id)\n         if not user:\n             raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n         return user\n     ```\n\n3. Implement consistent endpoint patterns:\n   - Standardize URL structure (e.g., `/api/v1/{resource}/{id}`)\n   - Use consistent HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) for CRUD operations\n   - Implement pagination, filtering, and sorting parameters uniformly\n   - Standardize request/response models using Pydantic schemas\n   - Document all endpoints with OpenAPI annotations\n\n4. Create a centralized error handling system:\n   - Implement exception handlers for common error types\n   - Create a standardized error response format:\n     ```python\n     # /app/api/errors/http_error.py\n     from fastapi import Request, status\n     from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n     \n     class AppError(Exception):\n         def __init__(self, status_code: int, detail: str, code: str = None):\n             self.status_code = status_code\n             self.detail = detail\n             self.code = code\n             \n     async def app_error_handler(request: Request, exc: AppError):\n         return JSONResponse(\n             status_code=exc.status_code,\n             content={\n                 \"error\": {\n                     \"code\": exc.code or \"internal_error\",\n                     \"message\": exc.detail,\n                     \"status\": exc.status_code\n                 }\n             }\n         )\n     ```\n\n5. Register all routers in a central API module:\n   - Create an API router registry to manage all routers\n   - Implement versioning support for future API changes\n   - Configure middleware for request logging, CORS, etc.\n   \n6. Update API documentation:\n   - Ensure all endpoints have clear descriptions\n   - Document expected request/response formats\n   - Include example requests and responses\n   - Document error codes and their meanings",
        "testStrategy": "1. Functional Testing:\n   - Create a comprehensive test suite covering all refactored endpoints\n   - Verify each endpoint returns the expected responses for valid inputs\n   - Test error handling by triggering various error conditions\n   - Ensure all HTTP status codes are appropriate for each scenario\n   - Validate that response formats match the defined standards\n\n2. Integration Testing:\n   - Test the interaction between routers and services\n   - Verify dependency injection works correctly\n   - Test authentication and authorization flows across endpoints\n   - Ensure middleware components function as expected\n\n3. Load Testing:\n   - Compare performance metrics before and after refactoring\n   - Verify that the refactored API maintains or improves response times\n   - Test the API under high load to ensure stability\n\n4. API Contract Testing:\n   - Use tools like Pact or Postman to verify API contracts\n   - Ensure backward compatibility if this is an existing API\n   - Validate OpenAPI documentation matches actual implementation\n\n5. Manual Testing:\n   - Review API structure for logical organization\n   - Verify consistent naming conventions across endpoints\n   - Check that error messages are clear and helpful\n   - Test API usability from a client perspective\n\n6. Validation Criteria:\n   - All endpoints are properly grouped by domain\n   - URL patterns follow consistent conventions\n   - Error responses have standardized format\n   - HTTP status codes are used appropriately\n   - API documentation is complete and accurate",
        "status": "done",
        "dependencies": [
          1,
          2,
          3
        ],
        "priority": "high",
        "subtasks": [],
        "section": "transkript"
      },
      {
        "id": 5,
        "title": "Implement CI/CD Pipeline with GitHub Actions",
        "description": "Set up GitHub Actions workflow for automated testing, security scanning, and deployment with quality gates to ensure code quality and secure deployment processes.",
        "details": "This task involves implementing a comprehensive CI/CD pipeline using GitHub Actions:\n\n1. Set up GitHub Actions workflow configuration:\n   - Create `.github/workflows/` directory\n   - Implement separate workflow files for different stages:\n     ```yaml\n     # ci.yml - For continuous integration\n     name: CI Pipeline\n     on:\n       pull_request:\n         branches: [ main, develop ]\n       push:\n         branches: [ main, develop ]\n     \n     jobs:\n       test:\n         runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n         steps:\n           # Setup steps\n           # Run tests\n           # Code quality checks\n     ```\n\n2. Implement automated testing:\n   - Configure unit test execution\n   - Set up integration test runs\n   - Implement code coverage reporting with minimum threshold (90%)\n   - Ensure tests run on all pull requests\n\n3. Add security scanning:\n   - Integrate SAST tools (e.g., CodeQL, Bandit for Python)\n   - Add dependency scanning (e.g., Dependabot)\n   - Implement container scanning if applicable\n   - Configure secret scanning\n   - Example configuration:\n     ```yaml\n     security-scan:\n       runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n       steps:\n         - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n         - name: Initialize CodeQL\n           uses: github/codeql-action/init@v2\n         - name: Perform CodeQL Analysis\n           uses: github/codeql-action/analyze@v2\n     ```\n\n4. Configure deployment workflow:\n   - Create staging and production deployment jobs\n   - Implement environment-specific configurations\n   - Add approval gates for production deployments\n   - Example:\n     ```yaml\n     # cd.yml - For continuous deployment\n     name: CD Pipeline\n     on:\n       workflow_run:\n         workflows: [\"CI Pipeline\"]\n         branches: [main]\n         types: [completed]\n     \n     jobs:\n       deploy-staging:\n         if: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'success' }}\n         # Deployment steps\n         \n       deploy-production:\n         needs: deploy-staging\n         environment:\n           name: production\n           url: https://production-app-url.com\n         # Production deployment steps with approval\n     ```\n\n5. Implement quality gates:\n   - Set up code quality checks (linting, formatting)\n   - Configure SonarQube or similar tool for code quality analysis\n   - Define minimum code coverage thresholds\n   - Establish performance benchmarks\n   - Block PRs/deployments if quality gates fail\n\n6. Configure branch protection rules:\n   - Require status checks to pass before merging\n   - Require PR reviews before merging\n   - Restrict who can push to matching branches\n   - Configure via GitHub repository settings\n\n7. Set up notifications:\n   - Configure Slack/Teams/Email notifications for pipeline failures\n   - Set up status badges in README.md\n\n8. Document the CI/CD process:\n   - Create documentation explaining the pipeline\n   - Include troubleshooting guides\n   - Document how to run tests locally to match CI environment",
        "testStrategy": "1. Workflow Configuration Verification:\n   - Validate all YAML files with a YAML linter\n   - Test workflows locally using act (https://github.com/nektos/act) if possible\n   - Verify all jobs and steps are correctly defined\n\n2. CI Pipeline Testing:\n   - Create a test PR with passing tests to verify the CI workflow runs successfully\n   - Create a test PR with failing tests to verify the CI workflow correctly blocks merging\n   - Verify code coverage reports are generated and accessible\n   - Check that linting and code quality checks are enforced\n\n3. Security Scanning Validation:\n   - Introduce a known vulnerability to verify security scanning detects it\n   - Test dependency scanning by adding a dependency with known issues\n   - Verify security reports are generated and accessible\n   - Confirm security issues block the pipeline as expected\n\n4. Branch Protection Testing:\n   - Attempt to push directly to protected branches to verify protection\n   - Create PRs without required reviews to verify they cannot be merged\n   - Verify status checks must pass before PRs can be merged\n\n5. Deployment Pipeline Verification:\n   - Test staging deployment with a minor change\n   - Verify staging environment receives updates automatically\n   - Test production deployment approval process\n   - Verify rollback procedures work as expected\n\n6. Quality Gates Validation:\n   - Submit code that violates quality thresholds to verify pipeline failure\n   - Check that quality reports are generated and accessible\n   - Verify quality metrics are tracked over time\n\n7. End-to-End Pipeline Testing:\n   - Run a complete cycle from PR creation to production deployment\n   - Measure pipeline execution time and optimize if necessary\n   - Verify all notifications are sent to the correct channels\n\n8. Documentation Review:\n   - Have team members follow documentation to verify clarity\n   - Ensure troubleshooting guides cover common failure scenarios",
        "status": "pending",
        "dependencies": [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ],
        "priority": "high",
        "subtasks": [],
        "section": "transkript"
