      {
        "id": 6,
        "title": "Implement Security Baseline with JWT Authentication and Authorization",
        "description": "Add JWT authentication, rate limiting, CORS configuration, and security headers. Implement user roles and permissions system to secure the application.",
        "details": "This task involves implementing a comprehensive security baseline for the application:\n\n1. JWT Authentication Implementation:\n   - Create a JWT authentication service:\n     ```python\n     class JWTService:\n         def __init__(self, secret_key: str, algorithm: str = \"HS256\", token_expire_minutes: int = 30):\n             self.secret_key = secret_key\n             self.algorithm = algorithm\n             self.token_expire_minutes = token_expire_minutes\n         \n         def create_access_token(self, data: dict) -> str:\n             to_encode = data.copy()\n             expire = datetime.utcnow() + timedelta(minutes=self.token_expire_minutes)\n             to_encode.update({\"exp\": expire})\n             return jwt.encode(to_encode, self.secret_key, algorithm=self.algorithm)\n         \n         def verify_token(self, token: str) -> dict:\n             try:\n                 payload = jwt.decode(token, self.secret_key, algorithms=[self.algorithm])\n                 return payload\n             except JWTError:\n                 raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid authentication credentials\")\n     ```\n   - Implement authentication middleware:\n     ```python\n     async def jwt_middleware(request: Request, call_next):\n         token = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\")\n         if token and token.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n             token = token.replace(\"Bearer \", \"\")\n             try:\n                 payload = jwt_service.verify_token(token)\n                 request.state.user = payload\n             except Exception:\n                 pass\n         return await call_next(request)\n     ```\n   - Create login/logout endpoints with token generation and validation\n\n2. Rate Limiting Implementation:\n   - Implement a rate limiter middleware using Redis or an in-memory store:\n     ```python\n     class RateLimiter:\n         def __init__(self, redis_client, max_requests: int = 100, window_seconds: int = 60):\n             self.redis = redis_client\n             self.max_requests = max_requests\n             self.window_seconds = window_seconds\n         \n         async def is_rate_limited(self, key: str) -> bool:\n             current = await self.redis.get(key)\n             if current is None:\n                 await self.redis.set(key, 1, ex=self.window_seconds)\n                 return False\n             if int(current) >= self.max_requests:\n                 return True\n             await self.redis.incr(key)\n             return False\n     ```\n   - Apply rate limiting to sensitive endpoints (login, registration, etc.)\n   - Implement tiered rate limiting based on user roles\n\n3. CORS Configuration:\n   - Set up CORS middleware with appropriate settings:\n     ```python\n     app.add_middleware(\n         CORSMiddleware,\n         allow_origins=[\"https://yourdomain.com\", \"https://app.yourdomain.com\"],\n         allow_credentials=True,\n         allow_methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\", \"PUT\", \"DELETE\", \"OPTIONS\"],\n         allow_headers=[\"Authorization\", \"Content-Type\"],\n     )\n     ```\n   - Configure different CORS policies for development and production environments\n\n4. Security Headers Implementation:\n   - Add middleware to set security headers on all responses:\n     ```python\n     @app.middleware(\"http\")\n     async def add_security_headers(request: Request, call_next):\n         response = await call_next(request)\n         response.headers[\"X-Content-Type-Options\"] = \"nosniff\"\n         response.headers[\"X-Frame-Options\"] = \"DENY\"\n         response.headers[\"Content-Security-Policy\"] = \"default-src 'self'\"\n         response.headers[\"Strict-Transport-Security\"] = \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\"\n         response.headers[\"X-XSS-Protection\"] = \"1; mode=block\"\n         return response\n     ```\n   - Configure Content Security Policy (CSP) appropriate for the application\n\n5. User Roles and Permissions System:\n   - Design and implement a role-based access control (RBAC) system:\n     ```python\n     class Role(str, Enum):\n         ADMIN = \"admin\"\n         MANAGER = \"manager\"\n         USER = \"user\"\n         GUEST = \"guest\"\n     \n     class Permission(str, Enum):\n         READ = \"read\"\n         WRITE = \"write\"\n         DELETE = \"delete\"\n         ADMIN = \"admin\"\n     \n     # Role-Permission mapping\n     ROLE_PERMISSIONS = {\n         Role.ADMIN: [Permission.READ, Permission.WRITE, Permission.DELETE, Permission.ADMIN],\n         Role.MANAGER: [Permission.READ, Permission.WRITE, Permission.DELETE],\n         Role.USER: [Permission.READ, Permission.WRITE],\n         Role.GUEST: [Permission.READ],\n     }\n     ```\n   - Create permission-checking decorators:\n     ```python\n     def requires_permission(permission: Permission):\n         def decorator(func):\n             @wraps(func)\n             async def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n                 request = kwargs.get(\"request\") or args[0]\n                 user = request.state.user\n                 if not user:\n                     raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Not authenticated\")\n                 \n                 user_role = user.get(\"role\", Role.GUEST)\n                 if permission not in ROLE_PERMISSIONS.get(user_role, []):\n                     raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=\"Not authorized\")\n                 \n                 return await func(*args, **kwargs)\n             return wrapper\n         return decorator\n     ```\n   - Update user model and repository to include roles\n   - Implement role assignment and management endpoints\n\n6. Environment Configuration:\n   - Store security-sensitive values in environment variables\n   - Create a secure configuration management system\n   - Implement different security profiles for development/testing/production\n\n7. Security Documentation:\n   - Document all security measures implemented\n   - Create developer guidelines for security best practices\n   - Document the RBAC system and how to use it correctly",
        "testStrategy": "1. JWT Authentication Testing:\n   - Unit test the JWT service:\n     - Test token generation with various payloads\n     - Test token validation with valid and invalid tokens\n     - Test token expiration handling\n   - Integration test the authentication flow:\n     - Test login endpoint with valid and invalid credentials\n     - Verify token is returned on successful login\n     - Test protected endpoints with and without valid tokens\n   - Test token refresh mechanism if implemented\n\n2. Rate Limiting Testing:\n   - Unit test the rate limiter service:\n     - Test counter incrementation\n     - Test window expiration\n   - Integration test rate limiting:\n     - Send requests exceeding the limit and verify 429 responses\n     - Verify rate limit headers are present in responses\n     - Test different rate limits for different user roles\n   - Load test to verify rate limiting under high traffic\n\n3. CORS Configuration Testing:\n   - Test CORS preflight requests (OPTIONS) from allowed origins\n   - Test requests from disallowed origins and verify they're blocked\n   - Verify correct headers are returned for CORS requests\n   - Test with various HTTP methods to ensure proper configuration\n\n4. Security Headers Testing:\n   - Create automated tests to verify all security headers are present on responses\n   - Use security scanning tools like OWASP ZAP to verify header effectiveness\n   - Test CSP by attempting to inject scripts and verifying they're blocked\n   - Verify HSTS is working correctly\n\n5. User Roles and Permissions Testing:\n   - Unit test the permission checking logic:\n     - Test each role against all permissions\n     - Test edge cases and invalid roles\n   - Integration test role-based access:\n     - Create test users with different roles\n     - Attempt to access endpoints with various permission requirements\n     - Verify correct 403 responses for unauthorized access\n   - Test role assignment and modification\n\n6. Security Vulnerability Testing:\n   - Run automated security scanning tools (OWASP ZAP, Snyk, etc.)\n   - Perform penetration testing on authentication and authorization systems\n   - Test for common vulnerabilities:\n     - SQL injection\n     - XSS vulnerabilities\n     - CSRF vulnerabilities\n     - JWT token vulnerabilities (algorithm confusion, etc.)\n\n7. End-to-End Security Testing:\n   - Create comprehensive test scenarios covering the entire security flow\n   - Test user registration, login, accessing protected resources, and logout\n   - Verify security measures work together correctly\n\n8. Documentation Testing:\n   - Review security documentation for completeness and accuracy\n   - Verify all security features are properly documented\n   - Test developer guidelines by having developers implement features following them",
