        "title": "Improve Test Coverage to 80%+ with Integration Tests and Performance Benchmarks",
        "description": "Expand test coverage from estimated 37% to 80%+ by adding unit tests, integration tests, fixtures, and performance benchmarks for critical application paths.",
        "details": "This task involves implementing a comprehensive testing strategy to significantly improve code coverage and quality:\n\n1. Analyze current test coverage:\n   - Use tools like pytest-cov or coverage.py to generate baseline coverage reports\n   - Identify critical paths and components with insufficient coverage\n   - Create a prioritized list of areas requiring additional tests\n\n2. Implement unit test improvements:\n   - Add missing unit tests for all repository implementations:\n     ```python\n     def test_user_repository_create():\n         # Arrange\n         user_data = {\"username\": \"testuser\", \"email\": \"test@example.com\"}\n         user_repo = UserRepository(db_session)\n         \n         # Act\n         new_user = user_repo.create(user_data)\n         \n         # Assert\n         assert new_user.id is not None\n         assert new_user.username == \"testuser\"\n     ```\n   - Create parameterized tests for edge cases and boundary conditions\n   - Implement mocking for external dependencies\n\n3. Develop integration test suite:\n   - Create test fixtures for database setup and teardown:\n     ```python\n     @pytest.fixture\n     def test_db():\n         # Set up test database\n         engine = create_engine(TEST_DATABASE_URL)\n         Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\n         connection = engine.connect()\n         transaction = connection.begin()\n         \n         yield connection\n         \n         # Teardown\n         transaction.rollback()\n         connection.close()\n     ```\n   - Implement integration tests for all repositories:\n     ```python\n     def test_user_repository_integration(test_db):\n         # Test full repository workflow with actual database\n         repo = UserRepository(test_db)\n         user = repo.create({\"username\": \"test_integration\"})\n         assert repo.get_by_id(user.id).username == \"test_integration\"\n     ```\n   - Add API endpoint integration tests using test client\n\n4. Implement authentication and security testing:\n   - Create tests for JWT token generation and validation\n   - Test authorization flows for different user roles\n   - Implement security-focused tests for rate limiting and CORS\n\n5. Establish performance benchmarks:\n   - Create benchmark tests for critical operations:\n     ```python\n     @pytest.mark.benchmark\n     def test_user_query_performance(benchmark):\n         result = benchmark(lambda: user_repository.find_by_criteria({\"active\": True}))\n         assert len(result) > 0\n     ```\n   - Measure and document baseline performance metrics\n   - Set up automated performance regression testing\n\n6. Implement CI integration:\n   - Configure test runs in the CI/CD pipeline\n   - Set up coverage reporting and quality gates\n   - Add performance benchmark tracking\n\n7. Create test documentation:\n   - Document testing approach and coverage goals\n   - Create guidelines for writing new tests\n   - Implement test naming conventions and organization",
        "testStrategy": "1. Coverage Analysis:\n   - Run coverage tools before and after implementation to verify improvement:\n     ```bash\n     pytest --cov=app --cov-report=xml --cov-report=term\n     ```\n   - Generate coverage reports showing at least 80% coverage for critical paths\n   - Verify coverage improvements across all major components\n\n2. Unit Test Verification:\n   - Run the complete unit test suite to ensure all tests pass\n   - Verify test isolation (tests don't depend on each other)\n   - Check edge cases and error handling coverage\n   - Validate mocking and test doubles are implemented correctly\n\n3. Integration Test Validation:\n   - Execute the integration test suite against a test environment\n   - Verify all repositories have corresponding integration tests\n   - Confirm database fixtures properly set up and tear down test data\n   - Test complete workflows across multiple components\n\n4. Performance Benchmark Verification:\n   - Run benchmark tests to establish baseline metrics\n   - Document performance results for key operations\n   - Verify benchmark tests are repeatable and consistent\n   - Set up performance regression detection\n\n5. CI Pipeline Integration:\n   - Confirm tests run successfully in the CI environment\n   - Verify coverage reports are generated and archived\n   - Test the quality gate functionality (build fails if coverage drops)\n   - Check that performance benchmarks are tracked over time\n\n6. Manual Review:\n   - Conduct code review of test implementations\n   - Verify test naming follows conventions and clearly indicates purpose\n   - Ensure tests are maintainable and follow best practices\n   - Check that test documentation is complete and accurate",
