      {
        "id": 8,
        "title": "Remove Script Duplicates from scripts/doubles/ Directory",
        "description": "Remove duplicate scripts in the scripts/doubles/ directory, ensuring only canonical versions remain in the codebase to reduce redundancy and maintenance overhead.",
        "details": "This task involves identifying and removing duplicate scripts to maintain a cleaner, more maintainable codebase:\n\n1. Analyze the scripts/doubles/ directory:\n   - Create an inventory of all scripts in the directory\n   - Identify the duplicate scripts and their canonical counterparts elsewhere in the codebase\n   - Document the functionality of each script to ensure proper preservation\n\n2. Identify canonical script locations:\n   - Determine where the canonical version of each script should reside\n   - Verify that canonical versions contain all functionality of the duplicates\n   - Create a mapping document linking duplicates to their canonical versions\n\n3. Update references:\n   - Search the entire codebase for references to scripts in the scripts/doubles/ directory\n   - Update all references to point to the canonical script versions\n   - Ensure import paths are correctly adjusted in all files\n\n4. Verification process:\n   - Create a verification script that confirms all functionality is preserved\n   - Run the verification script before and after changes to ensure equivalence\n   - Document any edge cases or special considerations\n\n5. Remove duplicates:\n   - After verification passes, remove the scripts/doubles/ directory\n   - Ensure build and test processes continue to function correctly\n   - Update documentation to reflect the new structure\n\n6. Implementation example for verification script:\n   ```python\n   def verify_script_functionality(duplicate_path, canonical_path):\n       \"\"\"\n       Compare the functionality of duplicate and canonical scripts.\n       Returns True if functionality is equivalent, False otherwise.\n       \"\"\"\n       # Import both modules\n       duplicate_module = importlib.import_module(duplicate_path)\n       canonical_module = importlib.import_module(canonical_path)\n       \n       # Compare function signatures and behavior\n       for func_name in dir(duplicate_module):\n           if func_name.startswith('_'):\n               continue\n               \n           if func_name not in dir(canonical_module):\n               print(f\"Function {func_name} missing in canonical version\")\n               return False\n               \n           # Test with sample inputs to verify behavior\n           # [Additional verification logic]\n       \n       return True\n   ```",
        "testStrategy": "1. Functional Verification:\n   - Create a test suite that exercises all functionality previously provided by scripts in the doubles directory\n   - Run tests before and after removal to ensure behavior remains identical\n   - Verify all edge cases and special conditions are handled correctly\n\n2. Reference Checking:\n   - Use static analysis tools to verify no references to removed scripts remain:\n     ```bash\n     grep -r \"scripts/doubles\" --include=\"*.py\" .\n     ```\n   - Ensure all imports and requires have been updated to canonical versions\n   - Verify no runtime errors occur due to missing scripts\n\n3. Integration Testing:\n   - Run the full application test suite to ensure no regressions\n   - Verify all components that previously used scripts from doubles directory function correctly\n   - Test startup, shutdown, and key application workflows\n\n4. Build Verification:\n   - Ensure the build process completes successfully without the doubles directory\n   - Verify deployment artifacts are generated correctly\n   - Confirm CI pipeline passes all stages\n\n5. Success Criteria Validation:\n   - Confirm scripts/doubles/ directory has been completely removed\n   - Verify no duplicate script functionality exists in the codebase\n   - Document the mapping between removed scripts and their canonical locations",
        "status": "done",
        "dependencies": [
          3
        ],
        "priority": "high",
        "subtasks": [],
        "section": "transkript"
      },
      {
        "id": 9,
        "title": "Refactor Large Component ActionItems.vue",
        "description": "Break down the 756-line ActionItems.vue component into smaller, focused components, extract reusable logic into composables and services to improve maintainability and readability.",
        "details": "This task involves refactoring the large ActionItems.vue component to improve maintainability, readability, and reusability:\n\n1. Analyze the current ActionItems.vue component:\n   - Identify distinct UI sections and responsibilities\n   - Map out data flow and state management\n   - Document business logic that can be extracted\n   - Identify reusable patterns for potential composables\n\n2. Create a component architecture plan:\n   - Design a hierarchy of smaller components\n   - Define clear interfaces between components\n   - Determine state management approach (props, emits, provide/inject)\n   - Plan for composition API usage\n\n3. Extract UI components:\n   - Create smaller, focused components for each distinct UI section:\n     ```\n     /components/action-items/\n       ActionItemsList.vue\n       ActionItemCard.vue\n       ActionItemFilters.vue\n       ActionItemHeader.vue\n       ActionItemDetails.vue\n       etc.\n     ```\n   - Ensure each component has a single responsibility\n   - Implement proper prop validation and defaults\n   - Use slots for flexible content composition\n\n4. Extract business logic into composables:\n   - Create reusable composables for common functionality:\n     ```\n     /composables/\n       useActionItemsFiltering.js\n       useActionItemsSorting.js\n       useActionItemsState.js\n       useActionItemsActions.js\n       etc.\n     ```\n   - Implement proper return values with reactive references\n   - Document each composable with JSDoc comments\n   - Ensure composables are testable in isolation\n\n5. Extract service layer for API interactions:\n   - Create service modules for data operations:\n     ```\n     /services/\n       actionItemsService.js\n       actionItemsApi.js\n       etc.\n     ```\n   - Centralize API calls and data transformations\n   - Implement error handling and loading states\n   - Add retry logic for failed requests if needed\n\n6. Refactor the main ActionItems.vue component:\n   - Import and use the new components and composables\n   - Remove duplicated code\n   - Simplify the template structure\n   - Ensure the component is under 300 lines\n\n7. Update imports and references:\n   - Update any components that import or use ActionItems.vue\n   - Ensure proper data flow between components\n   - Verify event handling works correctly\n\n8. Optimize performance:\n   - Implement lazy loading for components where appropriate\n   - Add memoization for expensive computations\n   - Use v-once for static content\n   - Consider using shallowRef for large objects",
        "testStrategy": "1. Code Quality Verification:\n   - Verify the refactored ActionItems.vue is under 300 lines\n   - Run linting tools to ensure code quality standards\n   - Check for proper component naming conventions\n   - Verify all components have proper prop validation\n\n2. Unit Testing:\n   - Create unit tests for each extracted component:\n     ```javascript\n     import { mount } from '@vue/test-utils'\n     import ActionItemCard from '@/components/action-items/ActionItemCard.vue'\n     \n     describe('ActionItemCard', () => {\n       it('renders correctly with props', () => {\n         const wrapper = mount(ActionItemCard, {\n           props: {\n             item: { id: 1, title: 'Test Item', status: 'pending' }\n           }\n         })\n         expect(wrapper.text()).toContain('Test Item')\n         expect(wrapper.find('.status').text()).toBe('pending')\n       })\n       \n       it('emits update event when action button clicked', async () => {\n         const wrapper = mount(ActionItemCard, {\n           props: {\n             item: { id: 1, title: 'Test Item', status: 'pending' }\n           }\n         })\n         await wrapper.find('.action-button').trigger('click')\n         expect(wrapper.emitted('update')).toBeTruthy()\n       })\n     })\n     ```\n   - Test all composables with unit tests:\n     ```javascript\n     import { useActionItemsFiltering } from '@/composables/useActionItemsFiltering'\n     \n     describe('useActionItemsFiltering', () => {\n       it('filters items correctly by status', () => {\n         const items = [\n           { id: 1, status: 'completed' },\n           { id: 2, status: 'pending' }\n         ]\n         const { filterByStatus } = useActionItemsFiltering(items)\n         const result = filterByStatus('completed')\n         expect(result.value).toHaveLength(1)\n         expect(result.value[0].id).toBe(1)\n       })\n     })\n     ```\n   - Test services with mocked API responses\n\n3. Integration Testing:\n   - Create integration tests that verify components work together:\n     ```javascript\n     import { mount } from '@vue/test-utils'\n     import ActionItems from '@/components/ActionItems.vue'\n     import { createTestingPinia } from '@pinia/testing'\n     \n     describe('ActionItems Integration', () => {\n       it('renders all child components correctly', () => {\n         const wrapper = mount(ActionItems, {\n           global: {\n             plugins: [createTestingPinia()]\n           }\n         })\n         expect(wrapper.findComponent({ name: 'ActionItemsList' }).exists()).toBe(true)\n         expect(wrapper.findComponent({ name: 'ActionItemFilters' }).exists()).toBe(true)\n       })\n     })\n     ```\n   - Test data flow between parent and child components\n   - Verify events are properly propagated\n\n4. Visual Regression Testing:\n   - Capture screenshots before and after refactoring\n   - Use tools like Storybook and Chromatic to verify visual consistency\n   - Test responsive behavior across different screen sizes\n\n5. Performance Testing:\n   - Measure component render times before and after refactoring\n   - Verify memory usage improvements\n   - Test with large datasets to ensure performance at scale\n\n6. Manual Testing:\n   - Create a checklist of all ActionItems.vue functionality\n   - Verify each feature works identically after refactoring\n   - Test edge cases and error states",
