            "id": 5,
            "title": "Refactor Main Component and Implement Service Layer",
            "description": "Refactor the main ActionItems.vue component to use the new components and composables, and implement a service layer for API interactions.",
            "dependencies": [
              "9.3",
              "9.4"
            ],
            "details": "1. Create service modules for data operations (actionItemsService.js, actionItemsApi.js)\n2. Implement API calls with proper error handling and loading states\n3. Add retry logic for failed requests\n4. Refactor the main ActionItems.vue to use new components and composables\n5. Remove duplicated code and simplify template structure\n6. Ensure the refactored component is under 300 lines\n7. Update any components that import or use ActionItems.vue\n8. Verify all functionality works as expected after refactoring",
            "status": "done",
            "testStrategy": ""
          }
        ],
        "section": "transkript"
      },
      {
        "id": 10,
        "title": "Refactor Large Component Companies.vue",
        "description": "Break down the 436-line Companies.vue component into smaller, focused components, extract reusable logic into composables and services to improve maintainability and readability.",
        "details": "This task involves refactoring the large Companies.vue component to improve maintainability, readability, and reusability:\n\n1. Analyze the current Companies.vue component:\n   - Identify distinct UI sections and responsibilities\n   - Map out data flow and state management\n   - Document business logic that can be extracted\n   - Identify reusable patterns for potential composables\n\n2. Create a component architecture plan:\n   - Design a hierarchy of smaller components\n   - Define clear interfaces between components\n   - Determine prop and event structures\n   - Plan for state management approach (Vuex, Pinia, or composition API)\n\n3. Extract UI components:\n   - Create CompanyList.vue for displaying the list of companies\n   - Create CompanyCard.vue for individual company display\n   - Create CompanyFilter.vue for filtering functionality\n   - Create CompanySearch.vue for search functionality\n   - Create CompanyForm.vue for add/edit operations\n   - Ensure each component is focused on a single responsibility\n\n4. Extract business logic into composables:\n   - Create useCompanyData.js for data fetching and manipulation\n   - Create useCompanyFilters.js for filtering logic\n   - Create useCompanySearch.js for search functionality\n   - Create useCompanyForm.js for form validation and submission\n\n5. Move API interactions to services:\n   - Create companyService.js for all API calls related to companies\n   - Implement proper error handling and loading states\n   - Ensure service methods are reusable across components\n\n6. Refactor Companies.vue to use the new components:\n   - Import and register all new components\n   - Replace sections of code with the new components\n   - Pass necessary props and handle events\n   - Ensure the main component is now primarily focused on composition and orchestration\n\n7. Implement proper data flow:\n   - Ensure one-way data flow principles are followed\n   - Use props for parent-to-child communication\n   - Use events for child-to-parent communication\n   - Consider using provide/inject for deeply nested components if necessary\n\n8. Add documentation:\n   - Document component interfaces (props, events)\n   - Add JSDoc comments to composables and services\n   - Include usage examples in component documentation\n\n9. Optimize performance:\n   - Implement lazy loading for components where appropriate\n   - Use v-memo or computed properties for expensive operations\n   - Ensure proper key usage in v-for loops\n   - Consider implementing virtual scrolling for large lists\n\n10. Refine and polish:\n    - Ensure consistent naming conventions\n    - Verify all components follow the same style patterns\n    - Check for any remaining code smells or anti-patterns",
        "testStrategy": "1. Code Quality Verification:\n   - Verify the refactored Companies.vue is under 300 lines\n   - Run linting tools to ensure code quality standards\n   - Check for proper component naming conventions\n   - Verify all components have proper prop validation\n\n2. Unit Testing:\n   - Create unit tests for each extracted component:\n     - Test rendering with various props\n     - Test event emissions\n     - Test conditional rendering\n   - Create unit tests for composables:\n     - Test all exported functions\n     - Test edge cases and error handling\n   - Create unit tests for services:\n     - Test API call methods\n     - Mock API responses for success and error scenarios\n\n3. Integration Testing:\n   - Test component interactions:\n     - Verify parent-child communication works correctly\n     - Test data flow between components\n   - Test the complete Companies feature:\n     - Verify all functionality works end-to-end\n     - Test with realistic data scenarios\n\n4. Visual Regression Testing:\n   - Capture screenshots before refactoring\n   - Compare with screenshots after refactoring\n   - Ensure UI appearance remains consistent\n\n5. Performance Testing:\n   - Compare rendering performance before and after refactoring\n   - Test with large datasets to ensure performance improvements\n   - Verify memory usage is optimized\n\n6. Manual Testing:\n   - Perform user flow testing for all company-related operations\n   - Verify all features work as expected in the browser\n   - Test across different screen sizes for responsive behavior\n\n7. Documentation Review:\n   - Verify all components are properly documented\n   - Check that composables and services have clear usage examples\n   - Ensure code comments are helpful and up-to-date",
        "status": "pending",
        "dependencies": [
          3,
          9
        ],
        "priority": "high",
        "subtasks": [],
        "section": "transkript"
      },
