      {
        "id": 117,
        "title": "Security: Audit Auth Column for API Surface",
        "description": "Review API Surface rows and set accurate authentication values (Bearer, permission:..., API Key) for all endpoints, with special attention to internal upload endpoints. Update DATA_FLOW_AUDIT_COMPLETE.md documentation accordingly.",
        "details": "This task involves a comprehensive security audit of the API authentication mechanisms:\n\n1. API Surface Authentication Review:\n   - Create an inventory of all API endpoints in the system\n   - For each endpoint, review the current authentication method specified in the Auth column\n   - Update the Auth column with accurate values based on the following categories:\n     - Bearer: For endpoints requiring JWT authentication\n     - permission:X: For endpoints requiring specific permissions (replace X with the actual permission name)\n     - API Key: For internal upload endpoints and other services requiring API key authentication\n     - None: For public endpoints that don't require authentication (review these carefully)\n\n2. Special Focus Areas:\n   - Internal upload endpoints: Ensure these are properly secured with API Key authentication\n   - Meeting participant endpoints: Verify proper Bearer token authentication with appropriate permissions\n   - Health check endpoints: Review security implications of authentication requirements\n   - Project user management: Ensure proper permission-based authentication\n\n3. Documentation Updates:\n   - Update the DATA_FLOW_AUDIT_COMPLETE.md document with:\n     - A summary of the authentication audit findings\n     - A table of all endpoints with their updated authentication requirements\n     - Any security recommendations or concerns discovered during the audit\n     - Timestamp and signature of the audit completion\n\n4. Implementation Verification:\n   - For any mismatches between documented and actual authentication requirements, create tickets for remediation\n   - Verify that the authentication mechanisms are properly implemented in the codebase\n   - Test a sample of endpoints to ensure authentication is enforced as documented",
        "testStrategy": "1. Documentation Verification:\n   - Create a checklist of all API endpoints in the system\n   - Compare the updated Auth column values against the actual implementation in the code\n   - Verify that DATA_FLOW_AUDIT_COMPLETE.md has been updated with accurate information\n   - Have a security-focused team member review the documentation for completeness\n\n2. Implementation Testing:\n   - For Bearer token endpoints:\n     - Test with valid tokens having correct permissions\n     - Test with valid tokens lacking required permissions\n     - Test with expired or invalid tokens\n     - Test with no authentication\n   - For API Key endpoints:\n     - Test with valid API keys\n     - Test with invalid API keys\n     - Test with no API key\n   - For permission-based endpoints:\n     - Test with users having the required permissions\n     - Test with users lacking the required permissions\n\n3. Security Validation:\n   - Perform a security scan of the API surface using automated tools\n   - Conduct manual penetration testing on critical endpoints\n   - Verify that internal upload endpoints are properly secured with API Key authentication\n   - Document any security vulnerabilities discovered and create tickets for remediation\n\n4. Final Review:\n   - Conduct a team review of the updated authentication requirements\n   - Verify that all authentication mechanisms align with the organization's security policies\n   - Ensure the DATA_FLOW_AUDIT_COMPLETE.md document is approved by the security team",
        "status": "pending",
        "dependencies": [
          23,
          109,
          110,
          111,
          112,
          114,
          115
        ],
        "priority": "medium",
        "subtasks": [],
        "section": "transkript"
      },
